# Kalman Filter Based EO Line-of-Sight Estimation

This project implements a Kalman Filter for estimating the Line-of-Sight (LOS) angle and angular rate of a target from noisy electro-optical sensor measurements.

The simulated EO sensor provides only angular measurements, while the Kalman Filter estimates both the target LOS angle and LOS angular rate.

## State Vector

The Kalman Filter estimates:

x = [ LOS Angle
      LOS Angular Rate ]

## Input

- Noisy EO angular measurement

The simulated measurement contains:

- Measurement noise
- High-frequency disturbances
- Short-duration measurement glitches

## Kalman Filter Structure

The algorithm performs:

1. State Prediction
2. Covariance Prediction
3. Innovation Calculation
4. Kalman Gain Calculation
5. Measurement Update
6. Covariance Update

## Outputs

- Estimated LOS Angle
- Estimated LOS Angular Rate
- Innovation
- Kalman Gain

## Performance Evaluation

The following signals are compared during simulation:

- True LOS Angle
- Noisy Sensor Measurement
- Kalman Estimated LOS Angle

The measurement error and estimation error can also be compared to evaluate the filtering performance.

This model demonstrates basic state estimation and sensor filtering techniques for EO tracking applications.
